{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md | sed -n '37,90p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-a-codex.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md | sed -n '37,90p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-a-codex.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# J2: the judge's next version, design for the council (2026-11-20, phase 1 steps 2–4)\n     2\t\n     3\t## What the census and the traces show\n     4\t- **The target.** 24 answers rejected by both readers (`census/CENSUS.md`). In about 16 of them the answer leaves the rung of its own\n     5\t  reference on a weak step. Main classes:\n     6\t  - O: overlapping amounts added (6);\n     7\t  - S: a figure of another scope taken as the value (6);\n     8\t  - E: an adjustment with no basis (5).\n     9\t- **The order of the answer (found at $0).**\n    10\t  - In all 48 stored answers of the probe set, the judge writes the fields in this order: `rung > reasons > cites > cites_views >\n    11\t    pushes > changed > why_changed > theme_pushes > reference > implied_outcome`. It chooses the rung first, and states the reference and\n    12\t    its own derivation last.\n    13\t  - The cause is code. `judging.schema_for` inserts `reference` and `implied_outcome` after `rung` in `required`. Its comment reads\n    14\t    \"after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\". But it appends them to the end of `properties`,\n    15\t    and the model writes the fields in `properties` order.\n    16\t  - D260 requires both fields but names no output order (council A's correction). The order of work is the reader brief's: first the\n    17\t    reference, then what the evidence implies, then the comparison.\n    18\t  - It is a plausible mechanism for the arithmetic that lands just across a boundary (7 of 24), and not yet a proven one. J2a tests it\n    19\t    alone.\n    20\t- **The model's own account** (`poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account/`, 24 continued conversations, $0.027). It names:\n    21\t  - \"State the implied figure … compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one\" (9);\n    22\t  - \"carries the guided growth forward\" (6);\n    23\t  - \"rumour … in proportion to their specificity\" (3);\n    24\t  - \"The rung is your forecast\" (3);\n    25\t  - \"discounted by default\" (1);\n    26\t  - \"Missing confirmation alone…\" (1).\n    27\t\n    28\t  Two answers concede the error: old-2 Q9 says \"I inferred a Q4 figure without enough evidence\"; new-2 Q31 says \"moved … without new\n    29\t  evidence\".\n    30\t- **Re-send noise.** The 48 stored requests are re-sent 3 times unchanged (arm v7, running). A target that flips on the re-send alone\n    31\t  is sampler noise and is reported apart.\n    32\t\n    33\t## Prompt audit (judging-v7 against the judgement ruler's reader brief and D260/D263)\n    34\t| Failure class | Request sentence that produces it | The standard's line | Verdict |\n    35\t|---|---|---|---|\n    36\t| Rung chosen before the derivation (all classes) | The schema's field order: rung first, `reference` and `implied_outcome` last. Sentence 10 lists the rung first | Reader brief: \"first establish what the market expected … then ask what the evidence implies, then compare the two\". D260: \"the answer states the reference and the implied outcome\", written before the reasons | **Contradiction (code)** |\n    37\t| O, overlapping amounts added | \"derive the outcome … check it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole …)\", applied only to dependencies, not to the judge's own sums | Reader brief and D260 (3): \"A part cannot exceed the whole it belongs to\"; \"the same claim … counts once\" | **Missing at its owner:** the identity is stated for dependencies, not for the judge's own arithmetic |\n    38\t| S, a figure of another scope as the value | \"a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share\", which covers periods and products, not companies, measures, or balance against flow | Ruler v1 §2′, the stage 3/4 analyst standard B: \"期间和定义要对上\" (period and definition must match). Extraction standard: a proxy of one aggregate is evidence for the same question, never its value | **Narrower than the standard** |\n    39\t| E, an adjustment with no basis | \"move when it crosses one\", together with \"once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay\" | Reader brief: \"a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it\"; \"Lean cautious, catch the increment\" | **Missing:** the shift is meant to be quantified, and the prompt never says that an unquantified adjustment does not cross |\n    40\t| W, talks taken as a likely completion (2) | \"third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity\" | Same line in the reader brief | **Misread**, 2 cases. Not targeted now |\n    41\t| R, a rung's own condition misapplied (2) | — | The rung text | **Misread**, 2 cases. Not targeted now |\n    42\t\n    43\t## The arms (revised after council A, `council-a-codex.md`; one lever each; every sentence sourced)\n    44\t| Arm | Change | Source | Characters |\n    45\t|---|---|---|---|\n    46\t| v7 | None, re-sent as stored | Noise control | 4,924 |\n    47\t| **J2a** | **Schema order only:** `properties` written as `reference, implied_outcome, reasons, rung`, then the rest unchanged. The system text is v7's, byte for byte, so the arm isolates order (council A: changing the wording too would not) | The reader brief's order of work; the code's own stated intent | 4,924 |\n    48\t| **J2b** | J2a, plus a two-row check at the end of the system text, before the rung is chosen: (1) **overlap**: before adding, ask whether one amount contains all *or part* of the other, and count a shared part once; (2) **scope**: a figure of another quantity is an input to adjust or a proxy to name, never the value as it stands, and say how it was adjusted | (1) \"a part cannot exceed its whole\" (reader brief, D260); (2) analyst standard B, \"期间和定义要对上\", and the extraction standard's proxy line. The form follows AGENTS §6 (a check at the end) | 5,562. +638, reason: the closing-check form; nothing is cut, since each existing sentence carries a D260/D263 behaviour |\n    49\t\n    50\t**Dropped after council A:**\n    51\t- **The first draft's row (3)**, \"an adjustment no item quantifies does not cross a boundary\". It could block guided growth, the discount on\n    52\t  untested targets and forecasts based on specific non-numeric evidence, which are D263 behaviours of the frozen gold. That is a return to\n    53\t  D260's v5 stickiness.\n    54\t- **The first draft's examples**, which mirrored the failing cases. The examples now come from other domains: a company's guidance and its\n    55\t  reported quarter; a lender's loan book and its committed loans.\n    56\t\n    57\t## The probe and the decision rule (written before any J2 send; revised after council A)\n    58\t- **Cases.** 24 targets, plus 24 controls that both readers supported, of the same draw and type (seeded). All 48 stored requests\n    59\t  rebuild byte for byte. The rebuild check compares content (sha over sorted JSON). Key order comes from production's own\n    60\t  `build_request` and `schema_for`; the arms reorder only `properties`.\n    61\t- **Sends.** Each arm × 48 cases × 3 repeats, at about $0.003 a call. Ledger `phase1.json`, $3.\n    62\t- **Reading, complete** (council A):\n    63\t  - every repeat of every case in the three arms, v7 re-send, J2a and J2b: 432 cards, plus 3 plants confirmed by a separate closed\n    64\t    reader;\n    65\t  - blind, shuffled, both families (`mark_cards`: Codex with memories off, Claude), debate rounds 1 and 2;\n    66\t  - every card in the same form: the answer, then \"Reference / Implied outcome / Reasons\";\n    67\t  - Claude reads every target that flips beside its material, and every control lost.\n    68\t- **One decision rule for an arm against v7's re-send:**\n    69\t  - (a) targets supported by both readers in at least 2 of 3 repeats: at least 12 of 24, and more than the v7 re-send;\n    70\t  - (b) controls lost (both readers reject in at least 2 of 3 repeats): no more than the v7 re-send loses;\n    71\t  - (c) agreement with the frozen judgement gold (gold-v1, `636c056d…`, the scorer's own rule, 51 requests of the r9-frozen-v108\n    72\t    draws, 3 repeats) no lower than the v7 re-send's. Every question that flips is read with its reasons.\n    73\t- **Falsifiers.**\n    74\t  - J2a moves no more targets than v7's re-send: order is not the mechanism.\n    75\t  - J2b fixes targets but fails (b) or (c): the check over-corrects. It stops there.\n    76\t- **Before the end-to-end slice: a production-path check** (council A).\n    77\t  - J2 and v7 run on identical inputs through `judging.round_of_judgements`, on a copy of one old store, over two consecutive days\n    78\t    with updates.\n    79\t  - It runs on the probe's questions and their dependants. J2 is patched into the harness; no package code changes.\n    80\t  - It checks: refusals by `check_answer`; the next day's request (the previous conclusion, the evidence shown from the citations);\n    81\t    dependants' consistency.\n    82\t- **The slice compares v7 and J2 on the same inputs.**\n    83\t  - Its arms are old reading with v7, old reading with J2, and c8 reading with J2.\n    84\t  - The first plan ran J2 in both arms; that is corrected in `PLAN.md`.\n    85\t\n    86\t## What this cannot show\n    87\t- **Opening, and the 17 matters never opened.** Phase 2.\n    88\t- **Effects across days.** A changed rung feeds the next day's previous conclusion. The end-to-end slice (plan step 7) shows those.\n    89\t- **A release verdict.** These cases are dev: they motivated the design. Acceptance is on a fresh window.\n    90\t\n    91\t## Out of scope for the council\n    92\tExtraction, opening, Steps 2–3, the frozen ruler's files, cost work.\n    37\t## Phase 1: the judge (J2)\n    38\t1. **$0 census.** Every answer of the 5 stored draws that the readers rejected or split, among the questions rated worth tracking. The\n    39\t   same frozen judge answered old-1..3 and new-2..3. Each is classified by mechanism, from the readers' reasons and the judge's own:\n    40\t   - overlap or arithmetic;\n    41\t   - range against the answer's own estimate;\n    42\t   - scope (other companies, year or measure);\n    43\t   - source weight (a company's own forecast over independent ones);\n    44\t   - missing material;\n    45\t   - the boundary between two ranges;\n    46\t   - other.\n    47\t\n    48\t   The largest class is the target.\n    49\t2. **Mechanism.** The whole judge request is read for 10 cases. The model's own account is taken on up to 10, at a cent each.\n    50\t3. **Design.** A prompt audit of judging-v7 against the judgement ruler (`ruler-v1.md`) and the standards. The levers are structural\n    51\t   first, for example a required estimate field whose chosen range code checks. Every sentence names its source, or goes to Alex.\n    52\t4. **Council A** on the design: an independent Codex read, then challenge rounds to consensus.\n    53\t5. **$0 checks.**\n    54\t   - Stored requests are rebuilt byte for byte.\n    55\t   - A synthetic answer passes every code check.\n    56\t   - J2 sits beside judging-v7. The production default and the frozen tests stay unchanged, apart from the code that admits a second\n    57\t     version.\n    58\t6. **A probe of cents.**\n    59\t   - The stored final requests of the failing cases are re-sent with J2, 3 times each.\n    60\t   - As many supported answers are re-sent as controls, which must not regress.\n    61\t   - Blind readers mark them, mixed with the archived answers.\n    62\t   - **Pass:** the decision rule in `DESIGN-J2.md` (targets, controls and the frozen gold, each against v7's re-send).\n    63\t7. **A production-path check, then the end-to-end slice in week 1** (revised after council A).\n    64\t   - First, J2 and v7 run on identical inputs through the judge's own round, on a copy of one old store, over two days with updates.\n    65\t   - Then the merge-test harness (the 09-06 copy) is extended to every open question, 09-07..09-20, on two old draws. Its three arms are\n    66\t     old reading with v7, old reading with J2, and c8 reading with J2.\n    67\t   - Readers mark every answer, and the 32 matters are counted as dev.\n    68\t   - The cost is estimated from archived tokens before the send.\n    69\t8. **Acceptance** on a fresh window, run once on Alex's word.\n    70\t\n    71\t## Phase 2: opening\n    72\t- A census of why the 17 matters were never opened, after phase 1's end-to-end slice. It is not designed now.\n    73\t\n    74\t## Limits\n    75\t- The frozen ruler is unchanged.\n    76\t- No paid send before the council and the $0 checks.\n    77\t- Phase 1 through step 6 costs about $1. Step 7's estimate is written before it runs.\n    78\t- Nothing is pushed or deployed.\n     1\t**Hold J2 before sending.** Putting the reasoning first is worth testing. J2b could make the judge ignore valid estimates, and the probe could miss that regression.\n     2\t\n     3\t- **Census.** I recounted 23 supported/insufficient splits, two supported/unsupported splits and 24 rejections by both readers. Five checks against the stored requests: **#4** repeats 28% without a denominator, an estimation error. **#6** has one tariff rumor and no usable timing evidence, so it tests how the judge handles missing material. **#12** uses a July 5 report to predict a later formal decision without explaining why that decision is likely. **#17** reasonably favors disclosed consideration over a media aggregate, but approximate inputs cannot securely place $24.9B below $25B. **#44** applies an uplift measured against consensus to a different revenue base. Also, setting aside **#41** hides a date error both readers noticed: six weeks versus roughly fourteen. [CENSUS.md:7](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md:7) · [rejected-answers.md:397](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/rejected-answers.md:397)\n     4\t\n     5\t- **Order.** Raw answers C003, C127 and C030 all put the forecast first and the derivation last, as did all 48. The schema appends the reasoning fields to `properties`. D260 requires both fields but specifies no output order. The reader brief specifies reasoning order. Early commitment could explain the arithmetic, but J2a changes both schema order and wording. Its result cannot isolate order. The archive hash also ignores key order. [judging.py:54](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:54) · [DECISIONS-log.md:3053](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3053) · [model.py:245](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:245)\n     6\t\n     7\t- **J2b.** Checking before choosing follows the brief. The overlap rule misses partial overlap, and its examples closely mirror the failures. The scope rule’s first sentence conflicts with using quarters, comparables and accounting inputs to derive the requested figure. The second sentence preserves proxies. Requiring an item to quantify the adjustment can block guided growth, discounts on untested targets and forecasts based on specific nonnumeric evidence. That risks restoring v5’s reluctance to move. [J2b.txt:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt:12) · [DECISIONS-log.md:3072](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3072)\n     8\t\n     9\t- **Probe.** Twelve repairs are possible on paper. In the partial v7 results, three of 27 target answers changed range, all on one question. Support still needs blind reading of every repeat, including unchanged ranges. The plan allows zero lost controls, the design two. I rebuilt all 51 July requests by archive hash, including one from July 13. Use the frozen score alongside per-question reasons. July omits the unjudged capex question, and the probe skips production validation. [DESIGN-J2.md:53](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:53) · [judge_probe.py:185](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:185)\n    10\t\n    11\t- **Plan.** Before the full slice, run one production-path comparison with v7 and J2 on identical inputs across two updates. Check whether changed citations alter what the next judgement sees and whether a changed conclusion reaches its dependants. The planned slice uses J2 in both arms. [PLAN.md:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md:63) · [judging.py:266](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:266)\n    12\t\n    13\tDISAGREE: Isolate answer order, preserve valid estimates, and require complete blind reading plus an early production-path comparison before advancing J2.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cmp src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2a.txt; diff -u src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt; for f in docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/*.order.json; do nl -ba \"$f\"; done; rg --files poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20 | cut -d/ -f4-5 | sort | uniq -c | head -75; tail -n 8 poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe-v7.log'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cmp src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2a.txt; diff -u src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt; for f in docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/*.order.json; do nl -ba \"$f\"; done; rg --files poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20 | cut -d/ -f4-5 | sort | uniq -c | head -75; tail -n 8 poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe-v7.log'","aggregated_output":"--- src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt\t2026-11-02 23:47:18\n+++ docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt\t2026-11-19 22:35:12\n@@ -9,3 +9,6 @@\n - Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n - Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n - changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\n+- Before you choose the rung, check the outcome you derived:\n+  (1) Overlap: before adding two amounts, ask whether one already contains all or part of the other; count any shared part once (a company's full-year guidance already contains the quarter it has just reported; a lender's loan book already contains the loans it has committed to fund).\n+  (2) Scope: a figure that measures something other than the question's quantity (other companies, another measure, a cumulative amount where the question asks for a balance at a date) is an input to adjust or a proxy to name, never the answer's value as it stands; say how you adjusted it.\n     1\t[\"reference\", \"implied_outcome\", \"reasons\", \"rung\", \"cites\", \"cites_views\", \"pushes\", \"changed\", \"why_changed\", \"theme_pushes\"]     1\t[\"reference\", \"implied_outcome\", \"reasons\", \"rung\", \"cites\", \"cites_views\", \"pushes\", \"changed\", \"why_changed\", \"theme_pushes\"]   1 account.log\n   1 account/T-new-2-Q11.json\n   1 account/T-new-2-Q20.json\n   1 account/T-new-2-Q26.json\n   1 account/T-new-2-Q27.json\n   1 account/T-new-2-Q31.json\n   1 account/T-new-2-Q4.json\n   1 account/T-new-2-Q5.json\n   1 account/T-new-3-Q23.json\n   1 account/T-new-3-Q26.json\n   1 account/T-new-3-Q4.json\n   1 account/T-old-1-Q28.json\n   1 account/T-old-1-Q45.json\n   1 account/T-old-1-Q7.json\n   1 account/T-old-2-Q16.json\n   1 account/T-old-2-Q29.json\n   1 account/T-old-2-Q6.json\n   1 account/T-old-2-Q9.json\n   1 account/T-old-3-Q14.json\n   1 account/T-old-3-Q23.json\n   1 account/T-old-3-Q3.json\n   1 account/T-old-3-Q33.json\n   1 account/T-old-3-Q37.json\n   1 account/T-old-3-Q41.json\n   1 account/T-old-3-Q7.json\n   1 cases.json\n   1 goldcases.json\n   1 ledger/phase1.attempts.jsonl\n   1 ledger/phase1.json\n   1 ledger/phase1.lock\n   1 probe-v7.log\n  83 probe/v7\nprobe T-old-1-Q7-1\nprobe T-old-1-Q7-2\nprobe T-old-1-Q7-3\nprobe C-old-1-Q34-1\nprobe C-old-1-Q34-2\nprobe C-old-1-Q34-3\nprobe T-old-2-Q16-1\nprobe T-old-2-Q16-2\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
