{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q31-3.json | sed -n '12,30p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '245,262p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2a.order.json\"","aggregated_output":"    12\t   \"split\": [\n    13\t    \"insufficient\",\n    14\t    \"unsupported\"\n    15\t   ]\n    16\t  }\n    17\t },\n    18\t \"repeat\": 3,\n    19\t \"arm\": \"v7\",\n    20\t \"answer\": {\n    21\t  \"rung\": 2,\n    22\t  \"reasons\": \"The reference is NVIDIA's “up to 2 gigawatts” target by 2027, which sits in rung 3. The target is a combined ambition, not a sized deployment schedule or set of binding commitments. The clearest quantified NVIDIA-specific commitment is IREN's signed 72MW collaboration; the other large figures are development or portfolio capacity without confirmation that they are DSX-dedicated and covered by binding deployment contracts. That supports a forecast below 0.5GW, so the outcome remains in rung 2.\",\n    23\t  \"cites\": [\n    24\t   \"e4318\",\n    25\t   \"e4499\",\n    26\t   \"e4708\",\n    27\t   \"e4709\",\n    28\t   \"e4710\",\n    29\t   \"e4711\"\n    30\t  ],\n   245\tdef request_identity(request):\n   246\t    \"\"\"The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation.\"\"\"\n   247\t    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   248\t    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   252\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   253\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   254\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   255\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   256\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   257\t    if hit:\n   258\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   259\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   260\t    started = time.time()\n   261\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   262\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n     1\t[\"reference\", \"implied_outcome\", \"reasons\", \"rung\", \"cites\", \"cites_views\", \"pushes\", \"changed\", \"why_changed\", \"theme_pushes\"]","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"**Hold the J2 sends.** The deck builder still samples eight unchanged-range answers per arm. That can hide better or worse reasoning within the same range. Require all 432 repeats to be accounted for, and count production refusals before scoring. [judge_probe.py:330](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:330)\n\n- **J2a.** I verified byte-for-byte prompt equality and that only the schema property order changes. J2a and v7 share an archive key, so a production check using a populated archive can silently replay v7. Start with empty, separate archives and verify the raw answer order. [model.py:245](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:245)\n- **J2b.** Row 2 allows comparable sizing, accounting identities and guided growth. Qualify “say how you adjusted it” so an unadjusted proxy can be explained without inventing a conversion. Row 1’s loan-book example assumes undrawn commitments are already in the balance. Make that conditional on what the lender reports. [J2b.txt:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt:12)\n- **Pass rule.** Keep 12/24 as a practical floor. In the 45 v7 target repeats I checked, four changed range. The only case with repeat changes still had a forecast below 0.5 GW paired with the 0.5–1.5 GW answer. Range changes cannot establish the v7 repair rate. Require a predeclared paired improvement by distinct question after blind reading. Count controls that drop from joint support to a split as losses too. [DESIGN-J2.md:68](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:68) · [v7 repeat:21](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q31-3.json:21)\n- **Production check.** The three-arm slice fixes the comparison. Choose a two-day case where an older citation controls what remains visible and a changed conclusion actually queues a dependant. [PLAN.md:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md:63) · [judging.py:41](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:41)\n\nDISAGREE: Make the deck complete, protect the comparison from cached answers, and lock the improvement rule before sending."}}
